<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan gets 410 mln rupees for Gulf war-hit.</title>
<headline>Pakistan gets 410 mln rupees for Gulf war-hit.</headline>
<dateline>ISLAMABAD 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>A welfare foundation for overseas Pakistanis said on Tuesday it had received 410 million rupees ($10.16 million) from a United Nations Compensation Commission for distribution among Pakistanis hit by the 1990-91 Gulf War.</p>
<p>A statement by the Overseas Pakistanis Foundation said it would begin on Friday the distribution of the amount among a total of 4,126 approved claimants for compensation for losses they suffered owing to the war, mostly in Kuwait after the Iraqi invasion there.</p>
<p>It asked the claimants living in Kuwait to contact the Pakistan embassy there.</p>
</text>
